  "narrative": "No obvious data leakage is present in these Welch comparisons: all exposures are measured predictors and cells meet the minimum-count rule, but several comparisons rely on small exposed cells and post hoc context splits, so I interpret them as dataset-specific associations only. The key feature_063 refinement H136 is decisive enough to accept in the supplied dataset: among core-flag-free participants excluding feature_027, feature_063=1 is associated with a lower outcome_001 by a signed +0.260 units, interval +0.182 to +0.338. This clears the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed direction and directly addresses the strongest overlap concern, because feature_027 was previously a much stronger negative driver. I accept H136 and request its independent validation. H133 also clears the threshold in the feature_002=0 complement (+0.250; lower +0.156), so I accept it as supportive marginal evidence, but keep H112 and H114 deferred because their direct full or core-free marginals are less clean with respect to feature_027/core-flag overlap. The formal feature_063-by-feature_002 interaction H131 is not supported (+0.114, interval includes zero and is below threshold), so the available evidence favors a feature_063 association that is not clearly concentrated in the feature_002-positive background, rather than the original feature_002-dependent hypothesis. H134 remains unresolved because, although its point estimate is large (+0.279), its lower bound is below threshold (+0.137) and the cleaned feature_002-positive stratum is small. The feature_027-by-feature_002 interaction H130 is also rejected as evidence of effect modification: its point is near threshold (+0.163), but the interval is wide and includes zero; this does not threaten the already validated full-population feature_027 association. For feature_003, the new battery mostly argues against a stable overall reverse association: H137 full population is below threshold (+0.139, interval crossing threshold), H138 core-flag-free feature_027-excluded is below threshold (+0.148; lower +0.093), H139 feature_063-excluded is only near-threshold (+0.164; lower +0.101), and the opposite isolated assay contexts H140/H141 are null. I therefore reject H137-H139 as overall/cleaned marginal claims, close H28 positive claim because it is opposite to the observed direction, and reject previously unresolved main contexts H94 and H102 whose validation intervals did not clear threshold. However, context-specific feature_003 evidence remains: the formal joint high feature_018/high feature_036 interaction H132 is strong (+0.779, lower +0.610) and H124 remains accepted as a very large selected mean-difference, though with only 22 exposed participants. H116 high feature_036 interaction and H104 high feature_036 mean difference remain contextually interesting but should not be upgraded beyond dataset-specific discovery evidence until further validation or more robust context tests. I registered a less extreme joint assay context proposal to test whether the feature_003 signal survives when both feature_018 and feature_036 are nonnegative rather than only high. All statements are associations in this supplied dataset, not causal or generalizable conclusions.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 appraise updated. Core validated marginals: feature_002=1 positive, feature_010=1 positive, feature_037=1 negative, feature_027=1 negative. Feature_027 is closed/validated. Feature_063: leading clean residual candidate is H136, accepted and requested for validation (core-flag-free, feature_027-excluded negative association, estimate +0.260, lower +0.182). H133 feature_002=0 complement also accepted but more marginal/confounded; H112/H114 left deferred because direct full or core-free marginals do not cleanly resolve feature_027/core-flag overlap. H121 remains accepted but active as a feature_002-positive marginal stratum, not the primary claim. Feature_063-by-feature_002 interaction H131 rejected; no clear feature_002 dependence. H134 cleaned feature_002-positive stratum remains unresolved/deferred. Feature_003: reject overall/cleaned marginal claims H137-H139, H94, H102, H28; isolated opposite contexts H140/H141 rejected. Remaining support is context-specific: H104 high feature_036 accepted, H115 high feature_018 interaction accepted, H124/H132 joint high assay context accepted/active but small-cell caution. Do not validate small H132 unless a future validation slot is explicitly prioritized. New proposal tests joint feature_018>=0 and feature_036>=0 mean difference in core-free population to see if feature_003 effect is less extreme than H124 but more specific than H104. Feature_040 interaction H142 rejected; keep feature_040-specific H95/H96 low priority. Broad screens remain active: rare binaries H125-H129, common binaries H28 now rejected but other common binaries remain, categorical H20-H24, feature_007 interactions H13-H16, core interaction battery H76-H87. Next analysis after H136 validation should either (1) if validated, accept feature_063 as clean residual and perhaps accept/cleanly close H112/H133/H121, then resume broad screens; or (2) if not validated, downgrade feature_063 to unresolved/discovery-only and prioritize fe